<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">11092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel's demolition of a tunnel network under the Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon was so large that the US Geological Survey logged it as a magnitude four point one tremor.</s> <s>Israeli forces took the ridge near Nabatieh last week, then destroyed two kilometres of tunnels they say held rockets, mines and a command post.</s> <s>When a demolition shows up on seismographs, it's measuring how much Lebanese land is being destroyed under an occupation that shows no sign of ending.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Amnesty International says Russia has trafficked foreign men into its war, luring them with ads for civilian work like driving jobs and then sending them to the front lines.</s> <s>Recruiters worked through agents and fake postings, then seized passports and phones once contracts were signed, a modern echo of empires filling their ranks with men from distant colonies.</s> <s>Their governments, from Brazil to Sri Lanka, have little leverage to bring them home... and Moscow denies the accusations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Sudan, five civil-society coalitions, among them the Darfur Women Platform, have rejected army chief Abdel Fattah al-Burhan's proposed national dialogue as political cover.</s> <s>When one warring party convenes the talks and picks the guests, it can claim a civilian mandate without civilian consent, and this time from the same movement that toppled Omar al-Bashir in twenty nineteen.</s> <s>The coalitions want the international Quintet mediation group to lead instead, while Darfur and Kordofan stay under siege from both the army and the Rapid Support Forces.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Colombia's earthquake has exposed who a relief system can't see: in Pereira, survivors who paid rent by the day have no lease in their name, so they can't register as official victims.</s> <s>The seven point four magnitude quake affected four hundred thousand people, but aid is allocated by proof of tenancy — and rooms rented by the night are where the poorest have always lived.</s> <s>Nearly four hundred people now shelter in a park, counted by volunteers but not yet by the state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Washington, the Department of Homeland Security wants to erase the sixty-day grace period that lets laid-off H-one-B workers look for a new sponsor.</s> <s>Most of those visas are held by Indian professionals, and like last month's six-figure visa fee, this change comes through rulemaking rather than a vote in Congress.</s> <s>If it survives public comment, a layoff becomes a deportation... and the employer who signs the termination letter will effectively decide whether a worker can stay in the country.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif has invited opposition leader Mehmood Khan Achakzai to consult on who'll lead the Election Commission.</s> <s>Article two hundred thirteen of the constitution requires the two men to agree, and in past deadlocks that consensus rule has left the commission without members for months.</s> <s>With Imran Khan's party marching on Islamabad, whoever they choose will referee an election that both sides already dispute.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Iran, a packet of tea now costs a day's wage, and families are borrowing against future income just to put food on the table.</s> <s>The rial's collapsed to a record low under American sanctions and war, and as Iraq learned in the nineteen-nineties, sanctions meant to squeeze a government usually hit its people's kitchens first.</s> <s>President Trump has tied the conflict to November's election, and Congress hasn't voted on it in seven months, so Iranian households face at least two more months of this.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A new study finds that cobalt exported from Congo's Copperbelt carries uranium that nobody declares.</s> <s>It's a strange echo of Shinkolobwe, the Congolese mine whose ore fed the bomb dropped on Hiroshima, and today's export paperwork tracks only the metal being sold, not the uranium riding in the same cargo.</s> <s>Mining communities absorb the radiation risk while refiners overseas receive the ore, and no agency has yet taken responsibility for counting it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Vietnam's trade surplus with the United States has hit a record.</s> <s>Factories flocked there during the first tariff war to escape duties on its giant northern neighbour, but many of their components still come from across that border, so each new record looks to Washington more like relabeled goods.</s> <s>Hanoi's famous bamboo diplomacy, bending toward both great powers without breaking, now faces tariffs designed to punish exactly the success it's built.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Argentina's monthly inflation has slowed again, to its lowest level in fourteen months, a striking turn for an economy that recently lived with triple-digit annual price rises.</s> <s>President Javier Milei's disinflation rests on a fiscal surplus carved out of pensions and public wages, in a country that's defaulted on its sovereign debt nine times.</s> <s>Pensioners have protested outside Congress every week, demanding incomes that keep pace... and the open question is how long a stabilisation paid for by the elderly can hold.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>UNICEF says one hundred seventy-one million students, roughly one in ten worldwide, lost class time to climate hazards in twenty twenty-five.</s> <s>Storms alone disrupted a hundred and nine million, more than floods and heatwaves combined, and three-quarters of those affected live in poorer countries whose schools weren't built to withstand either.</s> <s>A school that closes in a heatwave is really a verdict on the building... and children rarely make up the learning they lose.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Paris have found a hidden weak point in medulloblastoma, the most common malignant brain tumour in children.</s> <s>Its most aggressive form, driven by the <sub alias="mick">MYC</sub> gene, runs protein production in overdrive and survives only by keeping the cell's own stress brake switched off.</s> <s>Remove the regulator that holds that brake off, and the tumour's overdrive turns against it, though the work's still preclinical and no drug yet reaches the target.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At Umeå University in Sweden, scientists found that blocking a single transport system makes bacterial resistance to antibiotics collapse.</s> <s>Resistant bacteria survive by rebuilding their cell walls faster than drugs can damage them, and starving that repair line of building blocks tips the race back toward the medicine.</s> <s>It could revive cheap, decades-old antibiotics where newer drugs are unaffordable, in a world where resistant infections already kill more than a million people a year.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ukraine's new Shershen air defence system — the name means hornet — fires Soviet-era R-seventy-threes, American AIM-nine Sidewinders and British Asraam missiles from a single launcher.</s> <s>Most air defences tie one missile to one vendor's launcher, so when allies ration interceptors, the real bottleneck is integration, not the missiles themselves.</s> <s>Developers are still testing more missile types... and if they succeed, Kyiv can build its shield from whatever stock its partners happen to send.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chinese AI chipmaker Enflame roughly tripled on its Shanghai debut, and it's now worth twenty-seven point six billion dollars despite still losing money.</s> <s>American export curbs on Nvidia chips created that protected market, and Tencent, which owns eighteen percent of the company, supplied eighty-four percent of its revenue last year.</s> <s>Investors are pricing in demand that policy guarantees... and the nine hundred and twelve million dollars raised now has to prove the chips can compete on performance.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Anthropic, the maker of the Claude AI model, says five scientists sought its help with bioweapons work, including a blocked attempt to mutate the chikungunya virus for a suspected military program.</s> <s>Its threat report also details disrupted cyber-espionage and propaganda campaigns, and it comes shortly after a researcher resigned from the company.</s> <s>Yet the company remains both the only witness to this misuse and the only judge of its own safeguards, with no outside auditor checking either.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>